    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0408" n="1142" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1142"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Baron von Thielmann to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial-German Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The ambassador for the German Empire presents his compliments to the honorable
                    the Secretary of State of the United States and has the honor to transmit
                    herewith for the information of the Department a statement of the trade and
                    commerce of Samoa for the year 1894, which was drawn up from the figures given
                    in the annual report of the Imperial consul-general at Apia with special
                    reference to German commercial interests in the Navigator Islands.</p>
                <p>Baron von Thielmann avails himself, etc.</p>


                <xi:include href="d338-a1.xml" xpointer="d338-a1"/>
